---
title: v2.3 to v2.4
description: Promote the compiled-plan preview surface to the independent stable v2.4 release line.
---

Stable v2.4.0 promotes the features tested through v2.16.0-preview. These numbers belong
to independent release lines. The public removals were announced by v2.3.1 deprecations.

## Update composition and dispatch

Use public module builders with `AddGenerated()` / `AddGenerated(pattern)` and explicit
`Register<T>()` selections. Put executable plan generation in the composition root; libraries
can keep application selection methods and export selections with `ErgosfareGeneratePlans=false`.
Participants not selected at compilation cannot be introduced during startup or later.

Resolve `ICommandMediator`, `IQueryMediator` and `IEventMediator` from DI. Remove direct
mediator construction and calls to the deprecated mediator extension classes. Grouped
dispatch accepts `GroupSet`; collection expressions, implicit strings and `GroupSet.Of()`
replace the old string, array and enumerable overload families.

Replace two-parameter pre-interceptors with the single-message contract. Remove mediation
settings, `ForceMemoizedHandlers` and runtime registry/composition manipulation. Generated
plans determine participants and adapter calls at compilation; there is no reflective
execution fallback when a plan is missing.

## Treat diagnostics as part of composition

A known message/group without a main handler, including events, is a compilation error.
Dynamic groups use the generated filtering plan and report a missing handler at runtime.
Result adapters are compile-time-selected helpers, not DI services.

## Opt into experimental streams deliberately

`CommandStream<TChunk, TSelf>` and `QueryStream<TChunk, TSelf>` provide fluent, bounded
input with metadata on the concrete message. Existing experimental wrapper types remain.
Dispose input objects, pass cancellation to mediator dispatch and keep the request scope
alive throughout consumption. Output failures propagate to consumers/finals rather than
being swallowed by exception interceptors.

`ERGOEXP001–003` remain warnings for adapters, plugins and stream input even in the stable
package. The [streaming upload recipe](/ergosfare.docs/recipes/streaming-upload) provides a
complete application example with context handoff, cleanup and transport tests.
